One continuous game. Each civilization moves through the ages at its own pace, and [b]nothing resets[/b] at an age transition. A strong civilization can keep its lead and snowball.

[h2]How it works[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Your own age[/b]
One joined tech tree with two Breakthrough techs. Research the [b]Exploration Breakthrough[/b] and the [b]Modern Breakthrough[/b] to enter the next age, when you are ready. A small banner shows "Your age / World age".

[*][b]Civics have their own Breakthroughs[/b]
The joined civic tree has an Exploration and a Modern Breakthrough too. Research them with culture to open the next age's civics, also before your tech Breakthrough. Culture always has a use.

[*][b]The world still moves on[/b]
The world age changes at the normal time. Crises, legacy paths, treasure fleets, the Distant Lands and victories start with the world age, as in the base game.

[*][b]No reset[/b]
Cities stay cities, armies keep all their units, gold is not capped, old resources stay, and your techs, civics, policies and buildings stay.

[*][b]Content waits for your age[/b]
Later-age techs, units, buildings, unique items and civ abilities need that age's Breakthrough tech. Later-age civics need the civic Breakthrough. This stays true after the world moves on.

[*][b]Units upgrade across ages[/b]
For example Phalanx to Swordsman, and Pikeman to Line Infantry.
[/list]

[h2]Catch-up Research (optional)[/h2]
Set it in the game setup: [b]Advanced Options > Game Options > Catch-up Research[/b] (below Age Transition Impact). Choose before the game starts; you cannot change it later.

[table]
[tr][th]Setting[/th][th]After each world age transition[/th][/tr]
[tr][td]Off (default)[/td][td]No catch-up: full snowballing.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]+50%[/td][td]Techs and civics of earlier ages, and the Breakthrough into the new world age, cost two thirds.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]+100%[/td][td]They cost half.[/td][/tr]
[/table]

Only a civ that still needs those techs and civics gains from it, so it helps civs that are behind the world to catch up. AI civs get it too.

[h2]Recommended settings[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Age Transition Impact:[/b] Continuity.
[*][b]Start age:[/b] Antiquity.
[*][b]AI civ selection at age transition:[/b] Mirroring (default), or Current Civilization Persistence.
[/list]

[h2]New in 0.2.2[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Fix:[/b] in 0.2.1 no civ could research an Exploration or Modern civic. The civic tree now has its own Breakthroughs.
[*]Test of Time civic trees open with the civic Breakthrough. Syncretism (a legacy civ) needs the Breakthrough tech and works only in its own world age.
[*]Games saved with 0.2.1 continue with 0.2.2. The locked civics open at once.
[/list]

[h2]Status[/h2]
Playable, in testing. Full AI games pass all three ages at all four game speeds in automated tests. Human play through an age transition has had less testing. Please report problems in the comments.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]Version 0.2.2, built for Civilization VII 1.5.0.44, with the base game and DLC civilizations.
[*][b]Affects saved games:[/b] enable it before you start a new game. You can update the mod during a game from version 0.2.1.
[*]Replaces the game's age transition script. Other mods that change that script will conflict.
[*]Single player. Multiplayer is not tested.
[/list]

[h2]More information[/h2]
Documentation, source and known limits: [url=https://github.com/smithc/civ7-continuous-ages]github.com/smithc/civ7-continuous-ages[/url]
